					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-6414340#post-4257001</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-6414340/critter-profile:sampson#post-4257001</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Wed, 22 May 2019 01:54:06 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>Monteparnas</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>2926286</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>No, they are volunteers who like animals <strong>and</strong> know how to deal with them.</p> <p>But I think you're righter than me here. Mostly what really, really got me on this one was the time-displacement coming out of nowhere. It is too central to the concept for me to accept that they just arrived to this conclusion out of thin air.</p> <p>Since it will pull the string of the &quot;alternate timeline brother&quot;, I'm really not ok with it as is. I feel cheated as a reader, that is more it.</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-6414340#post-4256364</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-6414340/critter-profile:sampson#post-4256364</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Tue, 21 May 2019 15:48:47 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>DrAnnoyingDog</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>2425082</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>I have rarely seen Wilson's written as professional, and have never written them as such. Wilson's has always been cutesy to me, I mean they're a bunch of volunteers who like animals. That's their whole reason for existing.</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-6414340#post-4255321</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-6414340/critter-profile:sampson#post-4255321</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Mon, 20 May 2019 15:48:15 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>Monteparnas</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>2926286</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>No-vote for now. WWS strikes me like informal, but professional. This was effectively *unprofessional*, though. The writer deals with anomalies but seems at lost with any concept whatsoever outside liking animals, and the comments like *if they're happy, I'm happy!* are excessive, the general tone already made it warm enough.</p> <p>If it elaborates a little more on how they concluded &quot;time-displacement&quot; was at hand, and take off some of the lines that are just for cuteness sake of the writer, it will be pretty good.</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
